## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | 5 |
| **High** | 1 |
| **Medium** | 2 |

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test suite. Every public method is called, producing the 95% coverage metric, but almost nothing is actually verified. Bugs in pricing, search, CSV parsing, and removal would all slip through undetected.

---

### Critical Findings

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic)

The entire class follows the same anti-pattern: call a method, skip meaningful verification. 6 of 10 tests have **zero assertions** or only a trivial `Assert.IsNotNull` that would pass even if the returned data is completely wrong.

#### 2. No Assertion — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

```csharp
// BEFORE — proves nothing
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// FIX — verify the product is retrievable with correct values
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

#### 3. No Assertion — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 33)

Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
```

#### 4. No Assertion — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 39)

Never verifies the product is gone.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

#### 5. No Assertion — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 69)

A 10% discount is applied to two products — no price checked.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

#### 6. No Assertion — `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85)

Imports CSV but never confirms a product was created or that values were parsed correctly.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var imported = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(imported);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, imported.Price);
```

---

### High Finding

#### 7. Trivial Null-Check Assertions (lines 28, 51, 59, 81)

`GetProduct_Works`, `SearchProducts_Works`, `GetAllProducts_Works`, and `ExportToCsv_Works` only assert `IsNotNull`. They never verify **content correctness**.

```csharp
// BEFORE — passes even if search returns wrong products
var results = _catalog.Search("Widget");
Assert.IsNotNull(results);

